## Step 1 — Derive the package name from the lexicon
GRIMOIRE_DICTIONARY.md has a 3-tier table: `| 1337SP3@K | Grimoire | Orchestra | Definition |`
The **Orchestra** column is the plain-English naming tier. Pick ONE noun from
the Orchestra column that describes a pair of loops (HTTP-loop + direct-loop).
State your reasoning in one line.

If GRIMOIRE_DICTIONARY.md is unreadable, use the 1337_D1CT10N4RY.md lexicon
to construct a leet-safe name. Prefer an Orchestra-tier word if available.

Validate the chosen name against:
- lowercase ASCII [a-z0-9._-] only
- first char is a letter
- <= 100 chars
- no leading -/_/.
- not a Python stdlib module (ast, io, os, code, parser, types, copy,
  select, socket, signal, subprocess, token, uuid, json, base64, typing,
  logging, pathlib, tempfile, string, re, shutil, sys)
- if the name is >= 3 chars and you want PyPI safety, use:
    run: curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://pypi.org/pypi/<name>/json
  404 = free, 200 = taken. DO NOT use `curl -I https://pypi.org/project/<name>`
  — it follows redirects and always reports 200.

If the first choice fails any check, pick the next-best from the same tier.

## Step 2 — Target layout
Given derived name PKG:

~/deepcli/PKG/__init__.py
~/deepcli/PKG/loop.py         # from deepagent.py: _chat_once, loop, __main__ block
~/deepcli/PKG/tools.py        # TOOLS, DISPATCH, REQUIRED, execute, _log_tool_error
